{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WCw7h8ny4uRUAJSRfB2yUK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Claude bundle maintenance coordinates\n2\t\n3\tThis reference is delivered with the five-skill bundle. The bundle is the unit\n4\tfor installation, update and removal; siblings are dependencies, not optional\n5\tindependent packages. Its [scoped helper](../scripts/manage_install.py) validates\n6\texact source inventory and resolved local resources and checks owned installed\n7\tpopulation/content before update/removal.\n8\t\n9\tSelected method: `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\n10\t`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n11\tObserved host baseline: Claude Code 2.1.306. Actual resolved models and invocation\n12\tbehavior belong to individual trial evidence; package metadata does not prove\n13\thost qualification. Public tool profile:\n14\t`urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256\n15\t`a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`.\n16\tThe activation supplies the actual policy, principal and grant. Native\n17\t`results.conjoin` remains unsupported.\n18\t\n19\tRequirements-to-algorithm bindings: exact basis -> selected manager verification;\n20\tsource context -> public source acquisition; delegated operation -> actual scoped\n21\tcontract and returned evidence; effects -> current public write/reconciliation;\n22\tclosure -> qualified evidence and explicit consumer decision. Common method law\n23\tand a_c operation semantics remain with their owners. Source Product records and\n24\tthe installed method are external deciding inputs supplied by the engagement.\n25\tA host/tool/method or package change identifies the affected claims and tests;\n26\tretain valid unaffected evidence and re-evaluate affected paths on exact bytes.\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f0f958c-2912-4c30-85c1-81c66e3c8bcd","uuid":"1e01b4f4-e755-4752-9940-b01f29bc766e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:30:54.990Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-release-2ahz8bo2/claude/workspace/.claude/skills/stdo-release-install/references/maintenance.md","content":"# Claude bundle maintenance coordinates\n\nThis reference is delivered with the five-skill bundle. The bundle is the unit\nfor installation, update and removal; siblings are dependencies, not optional\nindependent packages. Its [scoped helper](../scripts/manage_install.py) validates\nexact source inventory and resolved local resources and checks owned installed\npopulation/content before update/removal.\n\nSelected method: `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\nObserved host baseline: Claude Code 2.1.306. Actual resolved models and invocation\nbehavior belong to individual trial evidence; package metadata does not prove\nhost qualification. Public tool profile:\n`urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256\n`a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`.\nThe activation supplies the actual policy, principal and grant. Native\n`results.conjoin` remains unsupported.\n\nRequirements-to-algorithm bindings: exact basis -> selected manager verification;\nsource context -> public source acquisition; delegated operation -> actual scoped\ncontract and returned evidence; effects -> current public write/reconciliation;\nclosure -> qualified evidence and explicit consumer decision. Common method law\nand a_c operation semantics remain with their owners. Source Product records and\nthe installed method are external deciding inputs supplied by the engagement.\nA host/tool/method or package change identifies the affected claims and tests;\nretain valid unaffected evidence and re-evaluate affected paths on exact bytes.\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WCw7h8ny4uRUAJSRfB2yUK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
