{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MyiNJsos6JaayCuHCfD8MY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: stdo-continuation\n3\tdescription: Use when resuming interrupted or prior governed STDO work in this repository, reconciling observed effects before retry, reporting truthful status and closure, or capturing qualification evidence. Keeps candidate availability, indeterminate assessment, and not-performed distinct. Not for unrelated tasks.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# STDO continuation, status, and evidence\n7\t\n8\tUse this skill on resume, after an interruption, when writing status, or when\n9\trecording evidence for qualification.\n10\t\n11\t## Resume and reconcile (SK-08, Q07, Q08)\n12\t\n13\tOn resume or after an interrupted effect:\n14\t\n15\t1. Acquire the material current state (re-observe the targets and read the\n16\t   retained records) before any retry.\n17\t2. Reconcile observed effects: if a target already changed, do not repeat the\n18\t   effect; a timeout does not prove rollback, and a repeated request must not\n19\t   duplicate an uncertain effect.\n20\t3. Retain unresolved obligations and still-valid evidence; invalidate only the\n21\t   reliance actually affected, each with its reason.\n22\t\n23\tTwo histories with identical candidate bytes are not interchangeable: one may\n24\tcarry a current accepted assessment and another an unresolved counterexample that\n25\tinvalidates its assessment. The retained obligation cannot disappear into a\n26\tcandidate-only summary — the continuations differ (Q07).\n27\t\n28\t## Status and closure (SK-09, Q09, Q10)\n29\t\n30\tState what was actually constructed, assessed, and decided: the exact subject,\n31\tthe basis, the evidence, and the remaining work.\n32\t\n33\t- Distinguish, with the correct predicate, the three outcomes: an exact\n34\t  **candidate is available**; an assessment was **performed but indeterminate**;\n35\t  an assessment was **not performed** (no result) and remains a residual. Never\n36\t  collapse these into one \"done\" or one \"exhausted\" verdict (Q10).\n37\t- Closure follows the applicable predicates and required dispositions — not a\n38\t  test count, not the mere occurrence of a review, not a fluent summary.\n39\t- An unsupported or unperformed case stays visible; it is never reported as a\n40\t  passing result.\n41\t- When a governed source or candidate materially changes, withdraw the affected\n42\t  reliance (including a prior passing review) and keep the missing reassessment\n43\t  open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable (Q09).\n44\t\n45\t## Capture evidence (SK-12, Q01, Q12)\n46\t\n47\tFor any qualification trial, retain the actual invocation, the acquired inputs,\n48\tthe outputs, the tool traces, the observed effects, the elapsed time, and any\n49\treported token or cost data. Measures that are unavailable stay **unknown** — do\n50\tnot invent them. Compare equivalent substantive information, and count retries,\n51\trepair, and review in the total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence for\n52\tthe exact case, host, and settings observed; it is not a success rate or a\n53\tgeneral benefit claim. A keyword or formatting check may establish structure but\n54\tnot successful method application.\n55\t\n56\t## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n57\t\n58\tWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `ACTIVATION.md` sections 5 and 7\n59\tand `FOUNDATIONS.md` (observation sufficiency) for restart, retained results, and\n60\tinvalidation; `ACTIVATION.md` section 3 for result and disposition;\n61\t`EVALUATION.md` section 7 and `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for test semantics\n62\tand actual-path proof.\n63\t\n64\t## Scope and limits\n65\t\n66\tThis skill records and reconciles; it does not itself qualify host behavior or\n67\tgrant acceptance.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f0f958c-2912-4c30-85c1-81c66e3c8bcd","uuid":"b13f15d5-5721-4cce-bf5e-6d00cc79b72f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:30:55.001Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-release-2ahz8bo2/claude/workspace/.claude/skills/stdo-continuation/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: stdo-continuation\ndescription: Use when resuming interrupted or prior governed STDO work in this repository, reconciling observed effects before retry, reporting truthful status and closure, or capturing qualification evidence. Keeps candidate availability, indeterminate assessment, and not-performed distinct. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO continuation, status, and evidence\n\nUse this skill on resume, after an interruption, when writing status, or when\nrecording evidence for qualification.\n\n## Resume and reconcile (SK-08, Q07, Q08)\n\nOn resume or after an interrupted effect:\n\n1. Acquire the material current state (re-observe the targets and read the\n   retained records) before any retry.\n2. Reconcile observed effects: if a target already changed, do not repeat the\n   effect; a timeout does not prove rollback, and a repeated request must not\n   duplicate an uncertain effect.\n3. Retain unresolved obligations and still-valid evidence; invalidate only the\n   reliance actually affected, each with its reason.\n\nTwo histories with identical candidate bytes are not interchangeable: one may\ncarry a current accepted assessment and another an unresolved counterexample that\ninvalidates its assessment. The retained obligation cannot disappear into a\ncandidate-only summary — the continuations differ (Q07).\n\n## Status and closure (SK-09, Q09, Q10)\n\nState what was actually constructed, assessed, and decided: the exact subject,\nthe basis, the evidence, and the remaining work.\n\n- Distinguish, with the correct predicate, the three outcomes: an exact\n  **candidate is available**; an assessment was **performed but indeterminate**;\n  an assessment was **not performed** (no result) and remains a residual. Never\n  collapse these into one \"done\" or one \"exhausted\" verdict (Q10).\n- Closure follows the applicable predicates and required dispositions — not a\n  test count, not the mere occurrence of a review, not a fluent summary.\n- An unsupported or unperformed case stays visible; it is never reported as a\n  passing result.\n- When a governed source or candidate materially changes, withdraw the affected\n  reliance (including a prior passing review) and keep the missing reassessment\n  open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable (Q09).\n\n## Capture evidence (SK-12, Q01, Q12)\n\nFor any qualification trial, retain the actual invocation, the acquired inputs,\nthe outputs, the tool traces, the observed effects, the elapsed time, and any\nreported token or cost data. Measures that are unavailable stay **unknown** — do\nnot invent them. Compare equivalent substantive information, and count retries,\nrepair, and review in the total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence for\nthe exact case, host, and settings observed; it is not a success rate or a\ngeneral benefit claim. A keyword or formatting check may establish structure but\nnot successful method application.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `ACTIVATION.md` sections 5 and 7\nand `FOUNDATIONS.md` (observation sufficiency) for restart, retained results, and\ninvalidation; `ACTIVATION.md` section 3 for result and disposition;\n`EVALUATION.md` section 7 and `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for test semantics\nand actual-path proof.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis skill records and reconciles; it does not itself qualify host behavior or\ngrant acceptance.\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MyiNJsos6JaayCuHCfD8MY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
